// HarnessCreateSessionWorkspaceTransfer creates an asynchronous, object-storage-backed transfer for payloads larger than the streaming path supports (> ~50 MiB). Bulk bytes never traverse harness-api: the client PUTs/GETs presigned DO Spaces URLs directly. Set `direction` to `upload` or `download`. - `upload`: responds 201 with `transfer_id` + `part_size`; the client then requests per-part presigned PUT URLs, uploads them to Spaces, and calls `commit`. - `download`: responds 202 with `transfer_id`; the client polls GET until `completed` and then fetches `download_url` from Spaces. Upload and cancel currently return 501 until the sandbox backend RPCs ship; download is live.
